## Test Helpers

```go
// Helper to create test app
func createTestApp() *fiber.App {
    app := fiber.New(fiber.Config{
        ErrorHandler: testErrorHandler,
    })

    setupRoutes(app)

    return app
}

// Helper to create JSON request
func createJSONRequest(method, url string, body interface{}) *http.Request {
    jsonData, _ := json.Marshal(body)
    req := httptest.NewRequest(method, url, bytes.NewReader(jsonData))
    req.Header.Set("Content-Type", "application/json")
    return req
}

// Helper to parse JSON response
func parseJSONResponse(resp *http.Response, v interface{}) error {
    return json.NewDecoder(resp.Body).Decode(v)
}
```

---

## Summary

- Use **app.Test()** to test handlers
- Use **httptest.NewRequest()** to create test requests
- Test **different scenarios** with table-driven tests
- Test **middleware** separately
- Create **integration tests** for full workflows
- Use **test helpers** to reduce boilerplate
